# Generation Flows and Processes

## Report Generation Flow

### Traditional Report Generation
1. **Extract Key Details** (Optional O1 path) - Pre-processes content to extract technical details
2. **Generate Marketing Report** - Transforms raw content into structured 3-part marketing reports
   - Introduction, business context relation, additional details
   - Focuses on technical details for developer audience
   - Outputs markdown wrapped in `<report>` tags

### Alternative O1 Model Path
- Uses pre-extracted key details as emphasis points
- Creates 4-part report with extra section for additional details
- Located in [src/agents/generate-report/prompts.ts](mdc:src/agents/generate-report/prompts.ts)

## Post Generation Flow

### 1. Business Context & Rules Setup
- **Business Context**: Defines target content (AI applications, agents, RAG, etc.)
- **Structure Instructions**: 5-word hook + 3-sentence body + 3-6 word call-to-action
- **Content Rules**: Casual tone, present tense, no hashtags, limited emojis
- **Validation**: Relevance criteria for AI applications and business context

### 2. Style Reference
- Uses 16 real post examples from [src/agents/generate-post/prompts/examples.ts](mdc:src/agents/generate-post/prompts/examples.ts)
- Provides style reference for AI to emulate

### 3. Post Generation Modes
- **Traditional Mode**: Reads marketing report and creates posts based on analysis
- **Raw Content Mode**: Analyzes raw content directly for key insights
- Takes notes on engagement strategies in `<thinking>` tags
- Outputs wrapped in `<post>` tags

## Thread Generation Flow

### 1. Plan Thread Structure
- Creates detailed outline with intro, body sections, conclusion
- Designs 3-10 post threads targeting AI enthusiasts and developers
- Outputs total post count in `<total-posts>` tags

### 2. Generate Individual Posts
- **First Post**: Engaging hook/intro under 280 characters
- **Body Posts**: Maintains coherence and flow with previous posts
- **Final Post**: Conclusion with call-to-action and summary
- **Style Rules**: Tweet formatting guidelines for readability

### 3. Thread Rewriting
- Edits threads based on user feedback while maintaining structure
- Reviews original thread and plan
- Applies user-requested changes with reflections/rules in mind

## Supporting Generation Features

### Content Curation
- Groups tweets by topic (new models/tools, UI/UX patterns, prompting strategies)
- Allows tweets in multiple groups
- Identifies specific products/tools mentioned

### Supervisor Decision Making
- **Report Grouping**: Identifies related reports for thread creation potential
- **Post Type Decision**: Analyzes complexity and interest level
  - New products/papers → threads
  - Smaller features → single posts

### Learning & Reflection
- **Reflection**: Analyzes user feedback patterns, compares original vs revised posts
- **Rule Updates**: Integrates new rules, combines similar rules, removes conflicts
- Enables continuous improvement based on human feedback
